  "retained_history": [
    "Initial all-target compilation and all sixteen new groups passed. First bootstrap filter retained 24 passes and one stale remaining-work failure; only that descriptive literal was changed after actual measurement.",
    "First baseline 1.88 benchmark wrapper used non-LTO linking and could not consume LLVM bitcode from the thin-LTO release library. The original plan, command and error remain retained; all four wrappers use the same corrected thin-LTO command before any timing.",
    "Production source and independent fixture remained byte-identical after initial review. Final source passed formatting, strict Clippy, both full suites and release build without further correction.",
    "Exactly one complete frozen timing run was performed: all 96 observations and pre/post byte bindings passed. No sample was excluded or retried."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Numeric quotas and reset sites remain unchanged. Cumulative charged heap is lower, leaving more logical author headroom. Already spent old object/order/tree blocks are not refunded.",
    "Fallible vector reservations and quota refusal precede map consumption. Postconsumption internal ordering failure discards the private initializer; reusable failed-map rollback is not promised.",
    "Shared permutation and exact owner guards make second-only malformed ordering unreachable through the production caller. First-map failure is exercised; both-local publication ordering is also reviewed in source.",
    "BTree and sort physical allocation failure remains an inherited infallible boundary; this is not comprehensive OOM recovery or production security.",
    "No Web API or standards coverage is added. Established unsupported/failing outcomes remain. Full web compatibility and the requested Chromium threshold remain unachieved."
  ],
